Checkpoint 12 owner validation
==============================

1. Validate code, configuration, dashboards, and systemd syntax:

    UV_CACHE_DIR=/tmp/webcam-uv-cache uv run pytest -q tests \
      --ignore=tests/test_upload.py
    docker compose --env-file .env --profile monitoring config --quiet
    systemd-analyze verify \
      deployment/systemd/checkpoint12-validation/*.service \
      deployment/systemd/checkpoint12-validation/*.timer
    git diff --check

2. Start monitoring and confirm infrastructure exporters:

    just monitoring
    docker compose --env-file .env --profile monitoring ps

Open Grafana through the existing port-3000 tunnel. Confirm the
Infrastructure health dashboard shows PostgreSQL, node, cAdvisor, and MQTT
targets up.

3. Inspect cleanup without deleting:

    just cleanup-spool 1 --dry-run
    just cleanup-spool 24 --dry-run --limit 10 --show-keys

Confirm backup/unknown objects are reported only as skipped and that eligible
counts and volumes are plausible. Perform a bounded deletion only after
reviewing its scope:

    just cleanup-spool 24 --limit 10

Confirm the Operational batch jobs dashboard records the run.

4. Create and verify a database backup:

    just backup-database --dry-run
    just backup-database

Confirm the returned key starts with `backups/postgresql/`, size is non-zero,
SHA-256 is present, and the dashboard records a successful backup. No restore
is part of checkpoint 12.

5. Review and install only the validation units:

    sudo cp deployment/systemd/checkpoint12-validation/webcam-checkpoint12-* \
      /etc/systemd/system/
    sudo systemctl daemon-reload
    sudo systemctl start webcam-checkpoint12-infrastructure.service
    sudo systemctl start webcam-checkpoint12-ingestion@windy.service
    sudo systemctl start webcam-checkpoint12-ingestion@fintraffic.service
    sudo systemctl start webcam-checkpoint12-ingestion@skaping.service
    sudo systemctl enable --now webcam-checkpoint12-cycle.timer

Confirm worker metrics appear on ports 8113, 8114, and 8115. Confirm Windy is
restricted to Denmark and each worker selects at most five jobs per epoch.

6. Observe at least two completed maintenance cycles:

    systemctl list-timers webcam-checkpoint12-cycle.timer
    systemctl status webcam-checkpoint12-cycle.service
    journalctl -u webcam-checkpoint12-cycle.service
    journalctl -u 'webcam-checkpoint12-discovery@*.service'
    journalctl -u webcam-checkpoint12-spool-cleanup.service
    journalctl -u webcam-checkpoint12-db-backup.service

Confirm cycles do not overlap, discovery is Windy then Fintraffic then
Skaping, failures do not suppress later jobs, cleanup uses one hour, and each
cycle creates a timestamped database backup.

Stop after validation and record owner approval. Full-scale production
orchestration and recovery drills belong to checkpoint 13.

The legacy `tests/test_upload.py` suite is excluded because its fixture still
patches the removed `api.main.IngestToPipeline` symbol. This is a pre-existing
test-maintenance issue in the legacy FastAPI upload path, not a checkpoint-12
failure.
